WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:09.260
This is the Korea Daily Brief from the CSIS Korea Chair, read by an AI voice. It's Thursday, November 12.

2
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:21.609
Three things today: Kim Jong Un visits a naval base under construction, South Korea's foreign minister flies to Beijing, and President Lee breaks ground on a major semiconductor investment.

3
00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:30.102
That naval inspection lands the same day North Korea's state media warns of action against a U.S.-led naval buildup in the region.

4
00:00:30.102 --> 00:00:39.380
And tomorrow, Foreign Minister Cho Hyun sits down with China's Wang Yi, a meeting that could shape Beijing's posture on North Korea diplomacy.

5
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:46.582
First, Kim Jong Un's inspection of a naval base under construction on North Korea's east coast.

6
00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:57.638
KCNA reported Thursday that Kim visited the site on November 11, ordering that construction be completed on schedule and to the quality standard set by the party central. N.K.

7
00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:08.694
News analysis places the site in Munchon, north of Wonsan, where base construction began more than 12 years ago. Satellite imagery showed work restarting there in August 2026.

8
00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:16.591
Senior officials Pak Jong Chon and Jo Yong Won accompanied Kim on the visit. The visit matters for more than one reason. N.K.

9
00:01:16.591 --> 00:01:24.677
News separately identified a second major east coast naval base project, suggesting simultaneous naval expansion on both coasts.

10
00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:41.419
That picture is reinforced by a 38 North analysis published today, which argues that North Korea's Choe Hyon destroyer represents a qualitative leap in surface naval power with direct implications for the ability to threaten South Korean and allied maritime assets.

11
00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:53.928
At the same time, KCNA carried a statement warning that North Korea would take action against the U.S.-led naval buildup in the region, a warning that runs directly alongside Kim's inspection visit.

12
00:01:53.928 --> 00:02:05.869
North Korean Foreign Minister Choe Son-hui added to that posture, releasing a commentary rejecting the G7 joint denuclearization statement from last week's Paris foreign ministers' meeting.

13
00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:16.672
Choe said North Korea's commitment to its nuclear buildup remains, in her words, "steadfast," and dismissed U.N. Security Council resolutions banning its weapons programs.

14
00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:28.170
What to watch: whether the Munchon base construction pace accelerates, and whether Pyongyang uses the APEC summit later this month as a diplomatic backdrop for any further signaling.

15
00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:40.736
Second, South Korea's foreign minister heads to Beijing. Foreign Minister Cho Hyun will make a two-day visit to Beijing starting Friday to meet Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi.

16
00:02:40.736 --> 00:02:49.020
Seoul's Foreign Ministry said Thursday the talks will cover North Korea-related issues, bilateral relations and regional matters.

17
00:02:49.020 --> 00:03:01.349
The visit follows Wang's invitation to Cho during Seoul talks in August, when Cho urged Beijing to play a constructive role in bringing North Korea back to dialogue. The timing is significant.

18
00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:13.101
Secretary of State Marco Rubio spoke with Wang Yi this week at China's request, covering President Trump's upcoming APEC travel to China and Xi Jinping's visit to Florida for the G20.

19
00:03:13.101 --> 00:03:18.623
That Rubio-Wang conversation reaffirmed a bilateral commitment to strategic stability.

20
00:03:18.623 --> 00:03:32.237
Meanwhile, a senior South Korean presidential official said Thursday that the chance of any U.S.-North Korea contact at APEC, before, during, or after the summit, was low, while declining to rule it out entirely.

21
00:03:32.237 --> 00:03:40.520
President Lee Jae-myung departs November 16 for ASEAN summits in Manila before the APEC summit in Shenzhen on November 18 and 19.

22
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:50.281
Cho's Beijing talks, then, land at a moment when Washington, Seoul, and Beijing are all calibrating their positions ahead of a crowded week of summitry.

23
00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:56.510
What Cho and Wang agree, or don't agree, on North Korea could set the tone heading into Shenzhen.

24
00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:09.951
Third, South Korea breaks ground on a major industrial expansion. President Lee Jae-myung attended the groundbreaking of three anchor facilities in the Chungcheong Mega Project on Thursday.

25
00:04:09.951 --> 00:04:21.479
They include a Samsung Electronics advanced semiconductor packaging fab in Asan, an advanced display production line, and an AI server high-performance substrate plant in Sejong.

26
00:04:21.479 --> 00:04:29.510
Six of eight anchor companies have begun active construction, just four months after the project was announced in July 2026.

27
00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:41.686
Lee said the Samsung chip packaging expansion in Asan alone would spur 30 billion dollars in additional investment. At the groundbreaking, Lee said: "What matters is action and execution."

28
00:04:41.686 --> 00:04:49.976
The full project value is cited at 392 trillion won. Samsung Electronics Chairman Lee Jae-yong attended alongside the president.

29
00:04:49.976 --> 00:05:04.160
The groundbreaking comes as South Korea's government is leaning heavily on large-scale industrial commitments to signal economic momentum. Six of eight anchor firms now actively building, that's the number to hold onto.

30
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:13.408
Now to Pyongyang. State media led today with Kim Jong Un's east coast naval base inspection, which you just heard in full.

31
00:05:13.408 --> 00:05:21.391
Alongside it, KCNA carried a warning that North Korea would take action against the U.S.-led naval buildup in the region.

32
00:05:21.391 --> 00:05:32.474
North Korean Foreign Minister Choe Son-hui also released commentary via KCNA rejecting the G7 denuclearization statement and affirming the nuclear buildup as steadfast.

33
00:05:32.474 --> 00:05:41.380
The bottom line from state media: a clear military-first message, with all recent weapons tests still absent from domestic KCNA output.

34
00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.379
The rest of the news, quickly.

35
00:05:44.379 --> 00:05:59.907
South Korea's Defense Minister Kang Shin-chul told the National Assembly budget committee Thursday that Seoul retains the upper hand in conventional forces, but North Korea is closing the gap in science and technology, citing drone flows from the Ukraine war.

36
00:05:59.907 --> 00:06:06.263
Seoul is seeking about 80 billion won, roughly 58 million dollars, for an integrated counter-drone system.

37
00:06:06.263 --> 00:06:21.912
On North Korean troops in Russia: former head of Ukraine's Center for Countering Disinformation Andrii Kovalenko assessed that another large-scale North Korean troop deployment to Russia this winter was unlikely, despite recent warnings from President Zelensky.

38
00:06:21.912 --> 00:06:33.183
The North Korean embassy in Beijing has been renovated, coinciding with the June Kim-Xi summit pledge to elevate bilateral ties and the opening of the New Yalu River Bridge in mid-October.

39
00:06:33.183 --> 00:06:47.033
Domestically, a special prosecutor raided the National Election Commission Thursday, with 25 investigators executing search and seizure at commission servers and two contractor offices, over alleged security-audit document forgery.

40
00:06:47.033 --> 00:07:00.883
The court administration chief said a threat to impeach former Prime Minister Han Deok-su over his potential release from detention was "inappropriate," saying that releasing him on statutory detention expiry is unrelated to guilt.

41
00:07:00.883 --> 00:07:10.177
The Supreme Court holds a second full bench hearing on Han's insurrection case on November 19, one day before his maximum detention expires on November 20.

42
00:07:10.177 --> 00:07:17.132
Lee Yong-cheol, former head of the Defense Acquisition Program Administration, was nominated as Minister of Justice.

43
00:07:17.132 --> 00:07:26.245
People Power Party opposition lawmakers said he would be unqualified unless he pledged that President Lee Jae-myung's indictment would never be dropped.

44
00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:35.958
Presidential spokesperson Kang Yu-jeong called a media report that President Lee had opposed former President Yoon Suk Yeol's impeachment "completely groundless."

45
00:07:35.958 --> 00:07:49.088
Foreign Minister Cho and Ukrainian Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha held their first face-to-face meeting since Seoul recalled its ambassador in October. South Korea's 2027 budget earmarks 100 million dollars for Ukraine.

46
00:07:49.088 --> 00:08:00.720
Seoul expanded the Cheonghae anti-piracy unit's operational zone from off Somalia to south of Oman in the Arabian Sea; the defense ministry submitted the revised motion to the National Assembly.

47
00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:12.002
A Gallup Korea poll taken November 3 to 5 put President Lee's approval at 41 percent. The Democratic Party stood at 36 percent, and the People Power Party at 28 percent.

48
00:08:12.002 --> 00:08:24.200
South Korea's industry minister pledged tighter government oversight of the Czech nuclear project as the construction contractor is replaced, saying there would be no disruption to the project.

49
00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:33.557
On Capitol Hill. An expert assessment warns that Democratic control of the House could slow legislative support for South Korea-U.S.

50
00:08:33.557 --> 00:08:43.568
350 billion dollar investment pledge and related cooperation frameworks, as Democrats have signaled skepticism toward deals struck under the Trump administration.

51
00:08:43.568 --> 00:08:55.680
Korean American Congressman-elect Dan Koh separately expressed concern about the U.S.-Korea alliance under Trump, saying Trump "shows more admiration and respect" for North Korea than South Korea.

52
00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:06.093
Beyond the region. President Lee will visit the Philippines for ASEAN-related summits before attending APEC in Shenzhen on November 18 and 19.

53
00:09:06.093 --> 00:09:14.657
A presidential official said the possibility of North Korea attending APEC or any U.S.-North Korea contact on the sidelines was low.

54
00:09:14.657 --> 00:09:26.270
South Korea and Indonesia are exploring joint arms export opportunities beyond the contested KF-21 cost-sharing dispute, seeking new frameworks for defense industrial cooperation.

55
00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:40.199
Finally, the markets. Seoul's main stock index, the KOSPI, closed Thursday down about six-tenths of a percent. Brent crude settled at about 92 dollars a barrel, down about half a percent.

56
00:09:40.199 --> 00:09:54.154
The dollar bought about 1,332 won, with the won slightly stronger on the day. The Bank of Korea's policy rate stands at 3.00 percent, set in October. That's the Korea Daily Brief for Thursday, November 12.

57
00:09:54.154 --> 00:09:58.510
The full text, with a link to every source, is in today's email.
